# Leaving torpor, and diablerie when it's blocked (rulebook, "Torpor", "Leave Torpor", "Diablerie",
# "The Blood Hunt"; zero-vtes rules-qa 48.3, 82.1, 114.1). A vampire in torpor can take no action
# but leaving it: undirected, so the prey and the predator may block; 2 blood if it succeeds.
# Blocked, there's no combat: a blocking vampire's Methuselah may diablerize it, and a blood hunt
# follows; otherwise the action fails and nothing is paid. A blocker may switch minions while its
# attempt is under way, which fails the first attempt.
seed 24
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
crypt A "Vera Nightfall" *12
library A "Iron Ward" *40
crypt B "Marek Hale" *12
library B "Iron Ward" *40
crypt C "Odile Fen" *12
library C "Iron Ward" *40
start

# Fast-forward: Alice has two vampires in torpor (4 blood and 1), Bob two princes, Carol a primogen.
A> transfer +4 A:uncontrolled:1
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> transfer +1 A:uncontrolled:1
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> move A:ready:1 torpor
A> move A:ready:1 torpor
B> transfer +4 B:uncontrolled:1
B> move B:uncontrolled:1 ready
B> transfer +4 B:uncontrolled:1
B> move B:uncontrolled:1 ready
C> transfer +5 C:uncontrolled:1
C> move C:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> next
A> next
expect turn 1 A minion

# In torpor, a vampire can't hunt, bleed or take any other action: only leave torpor.
reject:invalid A> hunt A:torpor:1

# Leaving torpor: Bob (the prey) and Carol (the predator) may block, and don't. It succeeds: the
# vampire is ready again, and pays 2 blood.
A> leavetorpor A:torpor:1
expect action leave-torpor A blocks
B> pass
C> pass
expect action leave-torpor A resolution
A> resolve success
log public The action succeeded
expect count A:torpor 1
expect card A:ready:1 blood 2

# The other has 1 blood: it can't pay, so the action fails.
A> leavetorpor A:torpor:1
B> pass
C> pass
reject:not-enough A> resolve success
A> resolve failure
expect count A:torpor 1

# Blocked. Bob tries with one prince, then switches to the other: the first attempt fails, and
# only one runs at a time (114.1). Nobody else does anything, so the block succeeds: no combat.
A> unlock A:torpor:1
A> blood +2 A:torpor:1
A> leavetorpor A:torpor:1
B> block B:ready:1
A> pass
B> block B:ready:2
log public B tries to block with Marek Hale instead of Marek Hale, whose attempt fails
A> pass
B> pass
C> pass
log public Marek Hale is locked: it blocked
expect waiting B:diablerie
# Bob doesn't diablerize: the action fails, and nothing is paid.
B> diablerize no
log public The action was blocked; nothing is paid
A> pass
expect action none
expect card A:torpor:1 blood 3

# Blocked again, by Bob's other prince, who diablerizes: the blood moves to him (up to his
# capacity of 6, so 2 of the 3), the victim is burned, and the blood hunt follows at once, polled
# from the acting Methuselah.
A> unlock A:torpor:1
A> leavetorpor A:torpor:1
B> block B:ready:1
A> pass
B> pass
C> pass
B> diablerize
log public Marek Hale diablerizes Vera Nightfall, taking 2 blood
expect card B:ready:1 blood 6
expect count A:torpor 0
expect count A:ashHeap 1
expect window polling minion
# Carol's primogen votes to burn him; Bob's other prince votes against. It fails, 1 to 2.
A> pass
B> vote against B:ready:2
B> pass
C> vote for C:ready:1
C> pass
A> pass
B> pass
A> pass
expect action none
expect count B:ready 2
